<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaEyeGlow_Stock.xml                      Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-11
  ============================================================================

  Companion to Defs/GeneDefs/JawaEyeColours.xml. That file gives our two
  authored eye genes a glow texture and a glow shader; this gives the SAME
  treatment to the stock gene BTD_Jawa also carries, so all three roll results
  match instead of one of them staying flat.

      Jawa_Eyes_HugeOrange     MoteGlow              (ours, in the GeneDef)
      Jawa_Eyes_HugeAmber      MoteGlowPulse         (ours, in the GeneDef)
      guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow   MoteGlowPulseLow      (here)

  Three shaders on purpose. One game load compares all three side by side, since
  the engine picks one gene per pawn and BTD_Jawa lists all three. Spawn twenty
  Jawa and roughly a third will wear each treatment.

  TransparentPostLight draws after the lighting pass, so the eyes hold full
  brightness in pitch dark without being additive. It is the conservative
  option and the expected fallback if the two Mote shaders misbehave on a pawn
  render node, which is not what they were written for.

  ⚠️ THIS EDITS ANOTHER MOD'S GENE. guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow belongs to Star Wars
  Xenotypes and is not Jawa-only, so any other xenotype carrying it also gets
  the glow. Checked against the resolved load set: it appears on BTD_Jawa and
  guy762_xenotype_jawa and nothing else, so the blast radius is Jawa either way.
  If a future update spreads it wider, this becomes a wider change.

  The texture swap is the load-bearing half. The donor art is flat (255,255,0)
  across the whole ellipse, so a <color> tint can only ever produce flat paint.
  jawaeyes_glow.png regrades the interior to a white-hot core with a rim at 62%,
  and because gene tinting MULTIPLIES, the core resolves to the full saturated
  colour and the rim resolves dark. That gradient is what reads as emission.

  SAFETY AND LOAD ORDER
  =====================
  Both ops are conditional on the exact node, so they self-disable if Star Wars
  Xenotypes restructures the gene. Star Wars Xenotypes is load 545 and
  Jawa_Patches is 564.

  Two ops rather than one because the gene has a separate render node per eye
  and each needs its own texPath and shader.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
    * Spawn ~20 Jawa and compare the three treatments. Pick one; make the other
      two match it.
    * Look at them at night and in an unlit room. That is the whole point.
    * If any reads as a flat white blob, the additive Mote shader is wrong for
      a pawn node; move that gene to TransparentPostLight.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[1]/texPath</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[1]/texPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <texPath>JawaEyes/jawaeyes_glow</texPath>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[1]</xpath>
          <value>
            <shaderTypeDef>MoteGlowPulseLow</shaderTypeDef>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[1]/drawSize</xpath>
          <value>
            <drawSize>0.35</drawSize>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[2]/texPath</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[2]/texPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <texPath>JawaEyes/jawaeyes_glow</texPath>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[2]</xpath>
          <value>
            <shaderTypeDef>MoteGlowPulseLow</shaderTypeDef>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[2]/drawSize</xpath>
          <value>
            <drawSize>0.35</drawSize>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
